WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.820
Two protons in a helium nucleus push each
other apart with an electric force of

2
00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:07.200
about 58 newtons.

3
00:00:07.250 --> 00:00:11.400
On something as light as a
proton, that is an enormous force.

4
00:00:11.450 --> 00:00:14.270
Yet the nucleus does not burst apart.

5
00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:16.250
Nor does it shrink to a point.

6
00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:21.520
So what stops it flying apart, and
what stops it collapsing in on itself?

7
00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:24.290
In this mission, you'll
explore the strong force,

8
00:00:24.340 --> 00:00:27.790
and how it changes with the
distance between nucleons.

9
00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:31.190
Then you'll set the strong force
against the electric force,

10
00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:34.200
and work out why a nucleus is stable.

11
00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:38.920
Your mission: explain why a nucleus
neither bursts nor collapses.
